metry x="40.0" y="996.0" width="82.0" height="72.0" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="mail" value="Resend + SMS&lt;br&gt;(notices)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1B1B2F;fillColor=#F2E7FB;strokeColor=#7E22CE;strokeWidth=1.5;shape=umlActor;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1152.0" y="758.0" width="82.0" height="86.0" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="howto" value='&lt;b style="font-size:11px"&gt;How to read this page&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• A stick figure is a PERSON or an outside SERVICE that uses the system.&lt;br&gt;• An oval is one thing they can do (a use case).&lt;br&gt;• A grey frame groups ovals. A line from an actor to a frame means the actor takes part in EVERY oval inside it. A line to one oval means&lt;br&gt;only that oval.&lt;br&gt;• A dashed purple arrow means "this oval always uses that one" (include) or "may add this step" (extend).&lt;br&gt;• The dashed outline is the edge of our website; anything outside it is not ours.' style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1B1B2F;fillColor=#FFFBEB;strokeColor=#D97706;strokeWidth=1.5;shape=note;size=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="1164.0" width="640.0" height="112.0" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="bn_t" value='&lt;b style="font-size:19px"&gt;U05  ·  Ministry team: department, events and follow-up&lt;/b&gt;' style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontColor=#000066;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=-2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40.0" y="72.0" width="1044.0" height="30.0" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="bn_s" value="UML: use cases   |   Three roles that look after people: Department Leader, Events Coordinator, Discipler   |   Phase 1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#64748B;strokeColor=n